-- title:
--   Powers of the weighted centre contract from the varpiₜ-chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a natural number $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ (`hℓ12`) and $\ell\mid M'$ (`hℓM'`). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\zeta=\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be (`hH₁`) the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ which (`hK`) is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb Q$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring which is a domain with $L$ as its fraction field and with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hϖ`) and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the chart algebra, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$. Let $y\subseteq C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: every ring homomorphism from $C$ to an algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ with kernel $y$ carries `jChartFin A ↥K j` (the element $j$) into [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (the Drinfeld-chart rigidity package; its clauses are summarised here) is imposed: for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk of $X$ at $z$ which is the germ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ (`hϖz`) and lies in the maximal ideal of that stalk (`hz`), and every point $y'$ of the affine chart `XFin A ↥K j` mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` (`hy'`) whose prime ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition (`hss'`), there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with maximal ideal generated by $\sigma\varpi$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $=X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v-f\,u)$, subject to: (i) $e$ carries the germ of each $a\in A$ to the constant $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ every level automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` — the condition that $\tau$ realises, after any embedding $\iota$ with $\iota\zeta=\exp(2\pi i/q)$, the substitution by `conjElemN q γ⁻¹` on quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ — preserves $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11}\equiv 1\pmod\ell$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for each such $\tau$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'$ there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ such that $\theta$ corresponds to $\tau$ through $e$ on germs of elements of $C$, fixes constants, has linear part $\sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the images of $X_0,X_1$, and satisfies $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$, $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ entrywise modulo the maximal ideal of $W$, $c\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma_{11}\equiv1\pmod\ell$, and $c\not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (v) a separation clause: two primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting at least one of the images of $X_0,X_1$ and containing the image of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, which contain elements with prescribed linear parts $a_1X_0+b_1X_1$ and $a_2X_0+b_2X_1$ ($a_i,b_i\in\mathbb Z$) modulo degree two, have distinct contractions to the stalk as soon as $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$; (vi) for a prime $P$ as above with linear part $X_0$, the germ of $a\in C$ lies in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of the maximal ideal of $A$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and for a suitable $a_0\in A$ the difference of this element and $a_0$ lies in $y'$ and has image in $S$ equal to a power series $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ for some $e_0\ge1$ whose degree-$e_0$ form is, at all pairs $(a,b)\in W^2$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb-ab^q$ in the maximal ideal, a unit.
--
--   Next, a single such datum is fixed: a point $z$ with $\varpi_z$ and `hϖz`, `hz`, a point $y'$ of `XFin A ↥K j` over $z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the supersingularity condition `hss'` and with $y'$ equal to $y$ (`hy'y`); a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$ with $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$, `hσ₁` saying the maximal ideal of $W_1$ is generated by $\sigma_1\varpi$, power series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S_1=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this datum exactly the list of clauses (i)–(vii) described above.
--
--   Finally, let $J\subseteq C$ be (`hJ`) the infimum of the set of those ideals of $C$ obtained as follows: for $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism of $K$ over $L$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` preserving $C$, take the contraction along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ of the contraction, along the composite of the germ map at $y'$, the map to the adic completion and $e_1$, of the ideal of $S_1$ generated by the images of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. Let $B$ be (`hB`) the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ underlying the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x\in K:\exists\,i\in J,\ x\cdot\varpi_t=i\}$, that is the blow-up chart $C[J/\varpi_t]$. Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). Four further packages are imposed: `hR1`, that $C\subseteq B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2`, that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that the elements of $L$ lying in $W$ are exactly those coming from $A$, that the maximal ideal of $W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that $y$ is the contraction to $C$ of the maximal ideal of $W$, and that $W$ is the set of quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h$ outside the maximal ideal of $W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here), that for any $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the contraction of the maximal ideal of $W$, compatible with $A\to k$, and equivariant for the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$ through an element $c\in\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\bar\gamma,c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with $c\neq1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; that level automorphisms attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is the image, under such an automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, of the contraction of the maximal ideal of $W$; that an element of $B$ sent into the maximal ideal of $W$ by all these automorphisms is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a level automorphism preserving $y$ preserves $W$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is: for every $n\in\mathbb N$ and every $c\in C$, if there exists $b\in B$ with $c=\varpi_t^{\,n}\,b$ in $K$, then $c\in J^n$.
--
--   This is the nontrivial half of the Rees-type contraction identity $J^n=C\cap\varpi_t^{\,n}C[J/\varpi_t]$ for the weighted centre $J$ of the supersingular blow-up chart, in the auxiliary frame where full level $\Gamma(q\ell)$ is replaced by a diamond condition at a guard prime $\ell\equiv11\pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_pow_mem_centre_pow_of_labelUnit_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_pow_mem_centre_pow_of_labelUnit_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd) in the construction of the integral model of the modular curve at a supersingular point, where the Drinfeld local chart is compared with the blow-up chart.
